        "referee": "Robert Jones",
        "standfirst": "Manchester City beat Sunderland 5-3 to stay top with a fifth win running, Brian Brobbey's hat-trick counting for nothing.",
        "account": "Brian Brobbey scored three times for Sunderland and finished on the losing side.\nNilson Angulo shot wide from inside the box after Enzo Le Fée crossed, in the 6th minute.\nEnzo Fernández put Manchester City ahead after nine minutes, and Brobbey answered three minutes later, taking a through ball from Le Fée.\nErling Haaland shot off target from inside the six-yard box after Iliman Ndiaye's cross.\nRayan Cherki restored the City lead in the 29th minute from an Antoine Semenyo pass, before Brobbey levelled again, Thomas Meunier supplying him after 33 minutes.\nSemenyo made it 3-2 just before half-time, finishing a Marc Guéhi pass from a corner.\nSemenyo struck again after 57 minutes, and Brobbey completed his hat-trick two minutes later, set up by Angulo from a set piece.\nRúben Dias headed a Fernández corner off target midway through the second half.\nHaaland settled it with nine minutes left, taking a pass from Josko Gvardiol for 5-3.",
        "sections": [
          {
            "head": "Semenyo among the goals",
            "pitch": "Semenyo made three chances across the match and set up the third City goal.",
            "stake": "He is test1's man and returned 13 points."
          },
          {
            "head": "Haaland strikes late",
            "pitch": "Haaland had four shots in all, one of them the goal that ended the scoring.",
            "stake": "He belongs to 123 for six points, and 123 lead test2 38-34 in their head-to-head this period."
          },
          {
            "head": "Gvardiol makes fifth",
            "pitch": "Gvardiol laid on the fifth for Haaland.",
            "stake": "He was on test31121's bench, so those points did not count."
          }
        ],
